/* base of a three-message exchange in OvlFunc_952_20085a4: the ROM holds it in
 * r5 across the whole cutscene and derives the other two with `add r0, r5, #2`
 * and `add r0, r5, #3`.  Written as a plain int, gcc pools all three ids
 * independently and never spends the register -- rematerialising a pool
 * constant is cheaper than a push/pop pair.  The symbol address is what makes
 * it derive.  0x2354 and 0x2355 are reached by arithmetic and are not named. */
_MSG_2352 = 0x2352;

/* Added while elevating OvlFunc_950_20085a8.  Same three-line-exchange shape as
 * _MSG_261c: base in a callee-saved register, `add r0, r6, #1` / `#2`. */
